+# Daily Grind account UI
+
+A responsive, dependency-free account page with passkey listing, rename and deletion dialogs, last-passkey warnings, empty/error states, and browser Signal API integration.
+
+## Static preview
+
+The supplied project has no server, database, authentication, or registered credentials. `index.html` therefore uses `data-source="demo"`. Its clearly labeled sample account persists edits in localStorage. Sample credentials **never** invoke WebAuthn or alter a real authenticator. Clear `daily-grind-passkeys-preview-v1` from localStorage to reset it. Other account tabs show preview content; site navigation retains the original destination URLs.
+
+## Connect a real signed-in account
+
+Set the body attribute to `data-source="api"`, populate the account identity/navigation from your authenticated server, and inject `<meta name="csrf-token" content="SESSION_CSRF_TOKEN">`. The UI calls:
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`
+- `PUT /api/account/passkeys/:id` with JSON `{ "name": "Work laptop" }`
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`
+
+Every successful response must contain the complete **current user's** credential list:
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "your-configured-registration-rp-id.example",
+  "userId": "amFtaWUtbGV3aXM",
+  "credentials": [{
+    "id": "bWFjYm9vay1wcm8",
+    "name": "Work laptop",
+    "provider": "iCloud Keychain",
+    "device": "laptop",
+    "registeredAt": 1789171200000,
+    "lastUsedAt": 1793923200000,
+    "current": true
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+IDs must be genuine unpadded Base64URL from registration, and `rpId` must match the configured registration RP. Dates are epoch milliseconds; `lastUsedAt` may be null. Derive optional provider information from registration AAGUID metadata; unknown providers use a generic fallback. `device` supports `laptop`, `phone`, or `key`; it is a display hint. Only mark `current` when the server can identify the authenticating credential.
+
+The backend must authenticate every request, enforce per-user ownership on every mutation, validate the CSRF token and request origin, validate trimmed names of 1–60 characters, and return 401 for expired sessions. Use HTTPS, secure session cookies, and `Cache-Control: no-store`. Do not trust a user ID from the client. There is deliberately no fallback to sample data when the real API fails. Passkey registration and primary authentication are outside this management UI.
+
+The browser receives `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` on initial load and after successful deletion, using only the authoritative server list and RP ID. Unsupported browsers continue to support account changes and show manual password-manager removal guidance. Signal failures are non-fatal and logged as warnings. Renaming a passkey changes its account label; it does not rename the user profile or invoke `signalCurrentUserDetails`.
+
+## Checks
+
+`npm test` runs Node's built-in test runner. No dependencies, build step, or server are required for those checks.
